## Minimalist and Clean-Girl Nail Art Worth Saving

Restraint is the hardest thing to get right in nail art, and <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/minimalist-nails/minimalist-nail-ideas'>minimalist nail design</a> proves it. Nothing here hides behind embellishment. Every line has to earn its place.

**1. The Single Line**

One thin line, drawn freehand across a bare or barely-there base, is the entire design. It works because it asks for precision rather than skill in the traditional sense, a steady hand matters more than years of training. The line typically sits diagonally across the nail bed or traces the edge of the cuticle, and either placement reads as intentional rather than accidental. Ask for it in black for contrast or a tonal shade for something quieter. It suits short and long nails equally, which is rare for a design this specific. At a salon, describe it exactly as one continuous line rather than a "simple design," since that phrasing gets you a more precise result.

