**2. Bare Canvas**

Negative space done at its most minimal, Bare Canvas leaves most of the nail untouched and lets a sheer or clear base carry the look. A small cut-out near the cuticle or tip is the only design element, often filled with a hint of colour or left completely open. This one photographs beautifully because the negative space catches light differently depending on the angle. It suits anyone whose job or lifestyle rules out anything too busy, since from a distance it reads as a clean, bare manicure. Ask for a gel base specifically. A regular polish base tends to show wear at the cut-out edge faster than gel does.

