**3. Tone on Tone**

This design skips colour contrast entirely and builds interest through finish instead, matte over glossy, or two shades of the same colour layered with a subtle line between them. The effect is closer to texture than pattern, which is what makes it read as sophisticated rather than plain. It works particularly well in neutral and skin-adjacent shades, where the tonal shift is felt more than seen. Request it by asking your tech for a matte top coat on part of the nail with a glossy finish on the rest, since that specific instruction gets the effect more reliably than describing the end result.

