## French Tip Nail Art, Reimagined

The <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/french-nails/french-tip-nail-designs'>French manicure</a> has not disappeared. It has just stopped being one thing. These three versions prove the classic tip is still the most flexible format in nail art.

**4. The Color-Dipped Tip**

Swap the traditional white line for a saturated colour and the entire manicure shifts mood without changing shape. A dipped tip in cherry red, cobalt, or acid green keeps the familiar French silhouette but reads current rather than classic. The line can be crisp and straight or slightly rounded depending on your natural nail shape, and either version holds up well since the colour sits in the same protected zone the white tip always occupied. This is one of the easier custom <strong>nail art ideas</strong> to request, since most techs already have the muscle memory for a French line, just not in white.

