## Abstract and Artistic Nail Art for the Bold

Abstract nail art rewards a nail tech with genuine hand-painting skill, so it is worth checking a portfolio before booking rather than assuming any tech can execute it well.

**10. Brushstroke**

Loose, visible brushstrokes in one or two contrasting colours make up the entire design, closer to a small abstract painting than a traditional pattern. The imperfection is the point. A too-precise version of this design actually reads as less confident than one with genuine movement in the line. It suits longer nail shapes best, almond or coffin, where there is enough surface for the brushwork to feel intentional rather than cramped. Bring a reference image of actual brushstroke nail art rather than describing it verbally, since the technique lives entirely in the execution.

