## Floral and Nature-Inspired Nail Art

Floral nail art has never really left, but the best current versions favour a few well-placed details over a full garden across every nail.

**13. Hand-Painted Bloom**

A single small flower, hand-painted rather than stamped or stickered, sits on one or two accent nails while the rest of the set stays simple. The texture and slight imperfection of hand-painted work is what separates this from a generic floral decal, and it is worth specifically requesting hand-painted over pre-made floral stickers for that reason. This design pairs particularly well with a <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/nails-by-color/green-nails'>sage or moss green base</a>, which grounds the floral detail rather than competing with it. Ask for the bloom on your ring finger only if you want a subtle version, or across two nails for something slightly more present.

