## Negative Space and Graphic Nail Art

Negative space designs tend to last well since they rely on precision rather than heavy product application, and the untouched nail underneath simply grows out like a normal manicure.

**15. The Cutout**

A deliberate gap in the polish, usually a geometric shape near the cuticle or centre of the nail, lets the natural nail show through as part of the design itself. It is one of the more technically demanding looks on this list, since a clean cutout depends entirely on precise line work rather than freehand looseness. The bare section should be buffed and sealed under the same top coat as the polished area, which keeps the whole nail wearing evenly. Ask your tech for a "negative space cutout" and be specific about the shape you want, circle, triangle, or straight-edged.

