## Print and Pattern Nail Art (Animal, Marble, and Beyond)

Pattern-based <strong>nail art ideas</strong> ask more of application technique than of the base colour choice, which is why the same marble or animal print design can look completely different from one tech to the next.

**17. Marble Effect**

Swirled, veined polish dragged through a wet base creates the look of natural stone, most commonly in white and grey tones though the technique works in nearly any colour combination. No two marble nails ever look identical, which is part of the appeal, each nail becomes genuinely one of a kind. The technique typically uses a fine brush or a dry marbling method dragged through wet polish before it sets. This is a strong choice if you want a design that reads sophisticated rather than trend-driven, since <strong>nail art ideas</strong> built around marble have held steady in popularity for years rather than cycling in and out.

