## Where This Leaves You

Twenty designs is a lot to hold in your head, and that was never really the point. The point was giving you <strong>nail art ideas</strong> specific enough to act on, a name, a reference, a reason a particular look works, so the next salon appointment does not start with "surprise me" and end with regret.

A pared-back set from the minimalist edit will always be the safer opening move if you are new to nail art. A chrome accent or a hand-painted bloom is where you go once you know what you like. And that last design, the one built to be found rather than searched for, is the one worth keeping in your back pocket for the appointment where you actually want your tech to take the lead.

Screenshot two or three of these before you close the tab. That is the whole edit doing its job.

